  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The state of Connecticut has $19.6B in federal contract obligations for FY2026 to date. The Department of Defense obligated $19.1B of that total. Obligations fell 44.1% year over year. Award activity shows 28,551 awards with an average award size of $688K. Year-to-date totals are partial because the fiscal year is ongoing, so the $19.6B figure does not represent a full-year total. Historical context shows prior fiscal-year obligations of $18.4B in FY21, $22.3B in FY22, $26B in FY23, $20B in FY24, and $35.1B in FY25. Engineering Services is the largest industry by obligations at $7.1B, followed by Ship Building and Repairing at $4.6B and Aircraft Manufacturing at $3.2B. ELECTRIC BOAT CORPORATION leads vendors with $11.6B in obligations, followed by RTX CORPORATION at $3.9B and SIKORSKY AIRCRAFT CORPORATION at $2.9B. This snapshot summarizes who is buying, who is selling, and which industries are receiving the most federal dollars in Connecticut so far in FY2026.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What drove Connecticut's federal contract total in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense drove the FY2026 total by obligating $19.1B. Engineering Services accounted for $7.1B of obligations and Ship Building and Repairing accounted for $4.6B. Obligations fell 44.1% year over year, and award activity shows 28,551 awards with an average award size of $688K."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which vendors and industries dominate federal contracting in Connecticut?",
        "body": "ELECTRIC BOAT CORPORATION dominated vendor obligations with $11.6B, followed by RTX CORPORATION with $3.9B and SIKORSKY AIRCRAFT CORPORATION with $2.9B. Engineering Services, Ship Building and Repairing, and Aircraft Manufacturing are the top three industries by obligations at $7.1B, $4.6B, and $3.2B respectively. Other notable vendors include HAMILTON SUNDSTRAND CORPORATION at $120M and LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION at $69.2M."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much federal contract money goes to Connecticut?",
      "a": "Connecticut receives $19.6B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The state has 28,551 awards so far with an average award size of $688K. Obligations fell 44.1% year over year. Historical obligations were $18.4B in FY21, $22.3B in FY22, $26B in FY23, $20B in FY24, and $35.1B in FY25."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies award the most contracts in Connecticut?",
      "a": "The Department of Defense awards the most contracts in Connecticut, obligating $19.1B. The Department of Homeland Security follows with $216M, the Department of Veterans Affairs with $149M, and the Department of Justice with $33.5M. Other buying agencies in the top ten include the General Services Administration at $23.4M and the Department of Health and Human Services at $21.5M."
